---
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

---

<ContentLayout
  title="Services: product development, rescue and modernisation, hosting and support, technical leadership | Freedom45"
  description="Freedom45 services: product development, rescue and modernisation of existing software, hosting and support, and technical leadership including fractional CTO, for startups, growing businesses and public bodies."
  activePage="services"
>
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Services</p>
    <h1>What we can do <span class="g">for you.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Bespoke software, from a first prototype to looking after it for years.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="service">
    <h2>Product development</h2>
    <p class="punch">Get it built.</p>
    <p>Websites, web apps, mobile and desktop apps, from a working prototype in weeks to a product people can rely on. Where a service needs both languages, we build Welsh and English in from the start, not translate at the end.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Prototypes and MVPs</li>
      <li>Web, mobile and desktop apps</li>
      <li>AI features</li>
      <li>Bilingual Welsh and English services</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="service">
    <h2>Rescue and modernisation</h2>
    <p class="punch">Get it back on track.</p>
    <p>Taking over software someone else built? We start with an honest review of the code: what's sound, what's risky and what to fix first, in plain English. Then we take it on.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Code and architecture reviews</li>
      <li>Performance and scaling</li>
      <li>Taking over software someone else built</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="service">
    <h2>Hosting and support</h2>
    <p class="punch">Keep it running.</p>
    <p>Launched isn't finished. We host it, keep it secure and up to date, and look after your users for as long as you want us to.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Hosting and monitoring</li>
      <li>Maintenance and security updates</li>
      <li>Customer support as a service</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="service">
    <h2>Technical leadership</h2>
    <p class="punch">Make the right calls.</p>
    <p>Not ready to hire a CTO? We can act as your technical lead: setting the direction, making the architecture calls and reviewing the code.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Fractional CTO</li>
      <li>Discovery and feasibility</li>
      <li>Technical strategy and roadmaps</li>
      <li>AI readiness</li>
      <li>Analytics and experimentation</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .service {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
  .service + .service { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  header + .service { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .service h2 { margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  .service .punch {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1e40af;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .service li { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .service .punch + p { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
</style>
